# behavior: the Rust interop contracts the retired codegen tests described through synthetic metadata hold over a real in-fixture crate: boxed variant payloads from every argument shape, a borrowed handle, owner-specialized and named-field constructors, a tuple-struct constructor, an owned mutable parameter, projected mutable tuple leaves and their unprojected control, two projected type arguments, a projection inside a trait method, a derived Component, an f32 boundary, keyword-spelled fields, a borrowing builder and client, a nested associated call, a trait method through its import, trait-qualified receiver modes, and a capturing closure passed to a crate method
